  "body": "The post-merge gate on main `1bd9298d6b1b5bb2858de6388f9b4d2691023249` is red (run 43587095462). Two suites failed.\n\n**Failure 1 - a real regression: the ui suites.**\nTest: `egui_app::tests::setup_mount_pages::each_setup_picks_its_own_machine_and_post_and_posts_one_file_per_mount`\nThe test panics at `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/setup_mount_pages.rs:101`. The post is refused. The message says:\n\n> post blocked - Setup1 (VMC 3-AXIS, Fanuc (built-in)): 18 warning(s): Face1: rapid move 0 travels below the clearance plane inside stock; Face1: move 19 cuts past the finish surface; ... (17 more move warnings)\n\nNothing wrong was posted - the refusal worked. The gouge check now judges this fixture toolpath as unsafe.\n\n**The cause is in the merge range `53a77c9dc..1bd9298d6`.**\nThe ui suites passed on `7c07e86830880fde86a575d86d34ff9fb89afd07` (run 43584872633). Only four merges landed between the two heads: #1622, #1634, #1640, #1644. All four change how a 2D cut is judged against the parts. One of them makes the check fire on this toolpath now.\n\n**Failure 2 - not a regression: the app import flake (#1605).**\nTest: `a_lowered_cap_refuses_the_same_face_at_once` failed at `crates/app/tests/import_step_guard.rs:36` with \"import did not finish within 30s\". The fix for #1605 merged at `141bc0696` (PR #1652). It moves that test to its own binary. No work is owed for this part.\n\nDone means: the `camcraft-ui --lib` suite is green on main. The fix names which of the four merges caused the warning. It then corrects the judgement, or shows that the fixture toolpath truly cuts past the finish surface and updates the fixture.\n",
